---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="T'au Empire Beginner's Guide — Warhammer 40k"
  description="New to the T'au? Learn the Greater Good lore, how the shooting army plays, how to paint battlesuits fast, and what to buy first."
>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="px-6 pt-16 pb-12 border-b border-[#2a2a35]">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <a href="/factions" class="text-sm text-[#4a4855] hover:text-[#8a8590] transition-colors mb-6 inline-block">
        ← All Factions
      </a>
      <div class="flex items-start gap-6">
        <div class="text-6xl">🎯</div>
        <div>
          <p class="text-[#c9a84c] text-sm font-semibold tracking-widest uppercase mb-2 font-display">Faction Guide</p>
          <h1 class="font-display text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold mb-4">T'au Empire</h1>
          <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-lg max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
            The most technologically advanced active civilization in the galaxy, 
            united under a philosophy of collective purpose — the Greater Good. 
            They shoot things from very far away with extreme efficiency, 
            pilot giant battlesuits, and are genuinely the closest thing to "good guys" in 40k.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Quick stats -->
      <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-3">
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Playstyle</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm">Pure Shooting</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Painting</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm text-green-400">Easy ✓</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Rules</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm text-yellow-400">Medium</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Starter Cost</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm">~$160–$230</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Lore -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-6">Who are the T'au?</h2>
      <div class="text-[#b8b4c0] leading-relaxed space-y-4 text-lg">
        <p>
          In a setting defined by ancient evils, dying empires, and ten-thousand-year-old grudges, 
          the T'au are startlingly young. Six thousand years ago they were primitive. 
          Now they have faster-than-light travel, plasma weapons, and giant walking battlesuits 
          piloted by warrior monks. The speed of their development is, to every other faction, 
          deeply suspicious.
        </p>
        <p>
          Their society is built around the philosophy of the <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Greater Good</strong> — 
          Tau'va in their language. The idea that every individual exists to serve the collective, 
          that cooperation achieves more than competition, and that the universe is better 
          when more beings join the cause. It sounds noble. In practice it means: 
          join us willingly, or be absorbed anyway.
        </p>
        <p>
          The T'au are divided into castes determined at birth. 
          The <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Fire caste</strong> are the warriors — disciplined soldiers 
          and battlesuit pilots. The <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Earth caste</strong> are engineers 
          who build everything. The <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Water caste</strong> are diplomats. 
          The <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Air caste</strong> pilot the ships. 
          Above all of them sit the <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Ethereals</strong> — 
          mysterious leaders who command absolute loyalty through means nobody fully understands.
        </p>
        <p>
          The strangest thing about the T'au: they have almost no presence in the Warp. 
          They can't use psychic powers. Chaos cannot corrupt them. 
          In a galaxy where everything is touched by the immaterium, 
          the T'au exist largely outside it — which makes them unique, 
          and makes the older, darker powers deeply uncomfortable.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Sept choice -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16 bg-[#0d0d0f]">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-2">Choose your Sept</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] mb-8 text-lg">
        Septs are the T'au equivalent of Space Marine Chapters — different homeworlds with different colors and special rules.
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-4">
        {[
          {
            name: "T'au Sept",
            colors: 'Bone White & Blue',
            swatch1: 'bg-gray-100',
            swatch2: 'bg-blue-600',
            painting: 'Easy',
            paintColor: 'text-green-400',
            desc: "The home sept — the original T'au world. Clean white/bone armor with blue markings. The default scheme and the most tutorials exist for it. Elegant, clinical, immediately recognizable.",
          },
          {
            name: "Sa'cea Sept",
            colors: 'Red & White',
            swatch1: 'bg-red-600',
            swatch2: 'bg-gray-100',
            painting: 'Easy',
            paintColor: 'text-green-400',
            desc: "A disciplined, traditional sept known for producing exceptional Fire Warriors. Bold red and white scheme that's easy to execute and looks striking on the table.",
          },
          {
            name: "Dal'yth Sept",
            colors: 'Blue-Green Camo',
            swatch1: 'bg-teal-600',
            swatch2: 'bg-cyan-400',
            painting: 'Medium',
            paintColor: 'text-yellow-400',
            desc: "Specialists in stealth operations. Blue-green urban camouflage with a more muted, tactical look. Slightly more complex to execute but very distinctive.",
          },
          {
            name: "Vior'la Sept",
            colors: 'Dark Red & Black',
            swatch1: 'bg-red-800',
            swatch2: 'bg-gray-900',
            painting: 'Easy',
            paintColor: 'text-green-400',
            desc: "Aggressive, hot-headed warriors — the most combat-focused sept. Dark red armor with black panels. Rules-wise they favor the aggressive Mont'ka doctrine. Easy and fast to paint.",
          },
        ].map(sept => (
          <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-5">
            <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
              <div class="flex gap-1 flex-shrink-0">
                <div class={`w-3 h-12 rounded-l ${sept.swatch1}`}></div>
                <div class={`w-3 h-12 rounded-r ${sept.swatch2}`}></div>
              </div>
              <div class="flex-1">
                <div class="flex items-center flex-wrap gap-3 mb-1">
                  <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-lg">{sept.name}</h3>
                  <span class="text-xs text-[#4a4855]">{sept.colors}</span>
                  <span class={`text-xs font-semibold ${sept.paintColor}`}>Painting: {sept.painting}</span>
                </div>
                <p class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm leading-relaxed">{sept.desc}</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Playstyle -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-6">How they play on the table</h2>
      <div class="text-[#b8b4c0] leading-relaxed space-y-4 text-lg mb-10">
        <p>
          T'au are the <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">premier shooting army in 40k</strong>. 
          Their weapons have longer range and better accuracy than almost any equivalent in the game. 
          Their goal every turn is simple: stay at distance, shoot everything, don't let anything 
          reach close combat.
        </p>
        <p>
          The army's core mechanic is <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Markerlights</strong>. 
          Pathfinders and drones illuminate targets with Markerlights — marked units can be
          targeted with improved effectiveness by the rest of your army that turn. 
          A well-markerlit target tends not to survive.
        </p>
        <p>
          Battlesuits are the army's centerpiece. 
          <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">XV8 Crisis Suits</strong> are versatile, 
          loadable with different weapons for different roles. 
          The <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Riptide</strong> is a towering walking fortress 
          that dominates the battlefield. The <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Ghostkeel</strong> 
          is a stealth battlesuit that appears behind enemy lines. 
          All of them are incredible models and the main reason people pick the faction.
        </p>
        <p>
          One unique rule: T'au units can <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Fall Back and Fire</strong>. 
          If something charges you and gets into melee, you can retreat next turn and still shoot. 
          For an army this bad at close combat, that's a lifeline.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-5">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-3 text-green-400">T'au are for you if...</h3>
          <ul class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm space-y-2">
            <li>✓ You want to win through precision firepower</li>
            <li>✓ You love giant mech suit models</li>
            <li>✓ You prefer clean sci-fi aesthetics over grimdark</li>
            <li>✓ You want the "least evil" faction in the game</li>
            <li>✓ You want a focused playstyle with one phase to master</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-5">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-3 text-red-400">Maybe look elsewhere if...</h3>
          <ul class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm space-y-2">
            <li>✗ You want a melee army — T'au in melee is a death sentence</li>
            <li>✗ You want grim, gothic, or horror aesthetics</li>
            <li>✗ You want psychic powers</li>
            <li>✗ You want to overwhelm with hordes</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Painting -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16 bg-[#0d0d0f]">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-2">How to paint T'au</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] mb-4 text-lg">Using T'au Sept (bone white + blue). The clean, flat armor panels are genuinely beginner-friendly.</p>
      <p class="text-[#b8b4c0] mb-10 leading-relaxed">
        T'au armor is the opposite of Orks and Guard — it's smooth, geometric, and clean. 
        That means no hiding mistakes behind "battle damage." 
        But it also means the techniques are simple: flat color, wash into recesses, 
        highlight edges. Each step is quick and the results are satisfying.
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-4 mb-10">
        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">1</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Spray Wraithbone</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">The warm cream base gives the bone-white armor a natural tint — better than pure white. Covers everything evenly.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">2</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Skeleton Horde Contrast on armor panels</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">A thin, warm beige contrast paint that shades into the recesses between armor plates. One coat gives you instant depth on the flat surfaces.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">3</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Talassar Blue Contrast on the accent panels</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">The blue sept markings — shoulder accents, helmet stripes, knee pads. Pick two or three areas per model and stay consistent. Less is more.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">4</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Leadbelcher on all weapons and tech</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Pulse rifles, fusion blasters, battlesuit arms. Metallic on everything mechanical. Follow with Nuln Oil for instant shadow.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">5</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Moot Green on sensor lenses and eye slits</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Every T'au helmet has a visor slit or lens array. A tiny stripe of bright green makes the model look alive and finished. One of the best payoff details in the game.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">6</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Drybrush Wraithbone on armor edges, base the model</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">A light edge drybrush restores brightness to the armor rims and panel edges. Clean, crisp highlight with minimal effort. Then a grey-blue base texture to match the T'au aesthetic.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#c9a84c] rounded-lg p-5">
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-2">Battlesuits paint differently than infantry</h3>
        <p class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Crisis Suits and Riptides have large, flat armor panels — more like painting a vehicle than a soldier. 
          They go faster than infantry but require neater work since the smooth surfaces 
          show mistakes more than textured Ork or Tyranid skin would. 
          Start with infantry to get the colors right, then tackle a battlesuit as your 
          first "hero" model. The payoff is significant.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- What to buy -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-2">What to buy first</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] mb-10 text-lg">One box, paint it, then decide if you want more infantry or your first battlesuit.</p>

      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#c9a84c] rounded-lg p-6 mb-6">
        <div class="mb-4">
          <span class="bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] text-xs font-semibold px-2 py-0.5 rounded font-display mr-2">Start Here</span>
          <span class="text-xs text-[#4a4855]">~$160</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-2">Combat Patrol: T'au Empire</h3>
        <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm mb-4 leading-relaxed">
          Includes an Ethereal (commander), Fire Warriors (core infantry), Pathfinders 
          (your Markerlight unit — essential to how the army works), and a Broadside Battlesuit 
          (heavy support). Covers every role you need to understand how T'au actually plays.
        </p>
        <a
          href="https://www.games-workshop.com/en-US/Combat-Patrol-Tau-Empire"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          class="inline-block bg-[#c9a84c] hover:bg-[#dfc070] text-[#111113] font-semibold px-5 py-2.5 rounded text-sm transition-colors font-display"
        >
          Buy from Games Workshop →
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-6 mb-6">
        <div class="mb-3">
          <span class="text-xs text-[#4a4855]">~$65 · the must-have second purchase</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-2">XV8 Crisis Battlesuits</h3>
        <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm mb-4 leading-relaxed">
          Three customizable battlesuits, each loadable with different weapon combinations. 
          The iconic T'au unit. Versatile, powerful, and genuinely stunning models — 
          this is the box that makes people fall in love with the faction. 
          Don't buy them until you've painted the patrol, but do budget for them.
        </p>
        <a
          href="https://www.games-workshop.com/en-US/XV8-Crisis-Battlesuits"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          class="inline-block border border-[#2a2a35] hover:border-[#c9a84c] text-[#b8b4c0] hover:text-[#c9a84c] font-semibold px-5 py-2.5 rounded text-sm transition-colors font-display"
        >
          View on Games Workshop →
        </a>
      </div>

      <!-- Paints -->
      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-6">
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-4">Paints you need (T'au Sept scheme)</h3>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          {[
            { name: 'Wraithbone Spray', use: 'Base coat — armor and battlesuits', required: true },
            { name: 'Skeleton Horde (Contrast)', use: 'Bone-white armor panels', required: true },
            { name: 'Talassar Blue (Contrast)', use: 'Sept color accent panels', required: true },
            { name: 'Leadbelcher', use: 'Weapons and mechanical parts', required: true },
            { name: 'Nuln Oil', use: 'Wash on metal areas', required: true },
            { name: 'Moot Green', use: 'Sensor lenses and eye slits', required: true },
            { name: 'Wraithbone (pot)', use: 'Edge drybrush on armor panels', required: false },
          ].map(paint => (
            <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class={`text-xs px-2 py-0.5 rounded mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 font-display ${paint.required ? 'bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113]' : 'border border-[#2a2a35] text-[#4a4855]'}`}>
                {paint.required ? 'Essential' : 'Optional'}
              </span>
              <div>
                <span class="text-sm font-semibold">{paint.name}</span>
                <span class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm"> — {paint.use}</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
        <p class="text-[#4a4855] text-sm mt-4 italic">~$38 total. The same paints cover infantry and battlesuits — the sept color is the only decision.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Cost breakdown -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16 bg-[#0d0d0f]">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-8">Honest cost breakdown</h2>
      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
        {[
          { item: "Combat Patrol: T'au Empire", cost: '~$160', note: 'Ethereal, Fire Warriors, Pathfinders, Broadside' },
          { item: 'Essential paints (6)', cost: '~$38', note: 'Spray + 2 contrast + metal + wash + green' },
          { item: 'Basing supplies', cost: '~$12', note: 'Grey-blue texture paint + tufts' },
          { item: 'Clippers + hobby knife', cost: '~$20', note: 'One-time purchase' },
          { item: 'Superglue', cost: '~$5', note: 'Battlesuits and multi-part kits' },
        ].map((row, i) => (
          <div class={`flex items-start justify-between px-5 py-4 gap-4 ${i % 2 === 0 ? '' : 'bg-[#111113]'}`}>
            <div>
              <p class="text-sm font-semibold">{row.item}</p>
              <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] mt-0.5">{row.note}</p>
            </div>
            <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] flex-shrink-0">{row.cost}</span>
          </div>
        ))}
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-5 py-4 bg-[#1f1d14] border-t border-[#c9a84c]">
          <p class="font-display font-semibold">All-in starter total</p>
          <span class="font-display font-bold text-[#c9a84c] text-lg">~$235</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-[#4a4855] text-sm mt-4 italic">
        Budget for Crisis Battlesuits (~$65) as your second purchase — they're the reason most people choose T'au 
        and the models that make the army feel complete.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="px-6 py-20 text-center">
    <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold mb-4">For the Greater Good.</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-lg mb-8">
        Pick your Sept, grab the Combat Patrol, and learn your Markerlights. 
        Then buy Crisis Suits and never look back.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
        <a
          href="/painting"
          class="inline-block bg-[#c9a84c] hover:bg-[#dfc070] text-[#111113] font-semibold px-8 py-4 rounded text-lg transition-colors font-display tracking-wide"
        >
          Painting Guide →
        </a>
        <a
          href="/quiz"
          class="inline-block border border-[#2a2a35] hover:border-[#c9a84c] text-[#b8b4c0] hover:text-[#c9a84c] font-semibold px-8 py-4 rounded text-lg transition-colors font-display"
        >
          Retake the Quiz
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
